FreeJ2ME-Plus's core starts its Java app in retro_init, with two pipes to
it, and ends the app in retro_deinit, but keeps the parent's ends of the
pipes open. A frontend that unloads the core between games never notices.
ZyperOS's Diatom keeps cores loaded and puts this one down with
retro_deinit after each game, so it would gain two open files with every
J2ME game. retro_deinit now closes them; the next retro_init opens new ones.

For ZyperOS, mk/build-freej2me.sh applies it; GPL-3.0 as the code it
changes.

--- a/src/libretro/freej2me_libretro.c
+++ b/src/libretro/freej2me_libretro.c
@@ -1526,6 +1526,13 @@
 		CloseHandle(hProcessSnap);
 #endif
 	}
+#if defined(__linux__) || defined(__APPLE__)
+	/* The parent's ends of the pipes javaOpen made: the next retro_init
+	 * makes two new ones, and a frontend that keeps the core loaded
+	 * between games would gain two open files with every game. */
+	if (pRead[0] > 2) { close(pRead[0]); pRead[0] = -1; }
+	if (pWrite[1] > 2) { close(pWrite[1]); pWrite[1] = -1; }
+#endif
 }
 
 void retro_reset(void)
